125
00:06:36,588 --> 00:06:40,388
Man, that was a close one. A few seconds more, it would have fallen in the river.

126
00:06:47,388 --> 00:06:50,108
I want to play with a cute little girl!

127
00:06:50,868 --> 00:06:52,028
Stop it, Shiro!

128
00:06:54,888 --> 00:06:56,548
Momo! Momo!

129
00:06:57,808 --> 00:07:00,988
I want to play! I want to play with the cute little girl!

130
00:07:01,308 --> 00:07:03,548
Come on, let's play! Let's play now!

131
00:07:06,548 --> 00:07:13,308
Come on, let's play!

132
00:07:16,888 --> 00:07:20,648
Hey, are you okay? How's your head? Did you bump it?

133
00:07:20,908 --> 00:07:22,628
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

134
00:07:22,628 --> 00:07:25,388
I didn't mean to make her cry!

135
00:07:25,388 --> 00:07:26,088
No!

136
00:07:26,088 --> 00:07:26,428
No!

137
00:07:46,428 --> 00:07:47,768
Look, Mama, we're home.

138
00:07:47,768 --> 00:07:49,728
Let's take care of those scratches.

139
00:07:51,368 --> 00:07:51,768
There.

140
00:07:52,848 --> 00:07:53,548
Okay, Momo.

141
00:07:54,008 --> 00:07:55,488
Do you know where the first aid kit is?

142
00:07:58,288 --> 00:07:58,688
Yeah.

143
00:08:04,048 --> 00:08:05,128
Alright, let me see.

144
00:08:08,728 --> 00:08:10,828
Looks like a little sand got in your wounds.

145
00:08:10,828 --> 00:08:18,968
Okay, now rinse your hand off.

146
00:08:20,228 --> 00:08:21,788
Water's too hot.

147
00:08:21,988 --> 00:08:22,428
Sorry.

148
00:08:22,748 --> 00:08:23,748
Just a little longer.

149
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:33,348
Alright, here we go.

150
00:08:34,628 --> 00:08:35,348
Let's see.

151
00:08:35,768 --> 00:08:36,088
Okay.

152
00:08:36,968 --> 00:08:38,828
Disinfectant and bandages.

153
00:08:39,248 --> 00:08:39,568
I know.

154
00:08:40,568 --> 00:08:41,968
No, I hope she's doing this.

155
00:08:51,968 --> 00:08:53,548
What's wrong?

156
00:08:53,548 --> 00:09:08,928
Hi, Mei!

157
00:09:15,928 --> 00:09:17,148
What's wrong?

158
00:09:20,348 --> 00:09:22,808
I'm really sorry about what happened today.

159
00:09:22,808 --> 00:09:24,228
It's not your fault.

160
00:09:24,808 --> 00:09:25,408
It's okay.

161
00:09:25,848 --> 00:09:27,368
Children have accidents all the time.

162
00:09:27,448 --> 00:09:27,928
It's normal.

163
00:09:28,308 --> 00:09:29,648
Don't worry, she's fine now.

164
00:09:29,888 --> 00:09:31,748
Momo's scratches don't hurt now.

165
00:09:37,748 --> 00:09:39,148
It's so bright.

166
00:09:39,528 --> 00:09:40,888
Hey, I'm thirsty.

167
00:09:41,448 --> 00:09:44,168
Can you give me some milk or something else, yummy?

168
00:09:44,508 --> 00:09:46,648
Ray barely touched any of his food at dinner.

169
00:09:47,208 --> 00:09:49,368
Guess he really felt bad about Momo getting hurt.

170
00:09:50,168 --> 00:09:52,628
I bet you really freaked him out with all of your crying.

171
00:09:53,088 --> 00:09:54,768
Momo didn't cry at all.

172
00:09:55,028 --> 00:09:57,188
Girl, I haven't had any dinner yet.

173
00:09:57,408 --> 00:09:59,108
That is a lie.

174
00:10:01,508 --> 00:10:02,228
Ray cried.

175
00:10:02,448 --> 00:10:03,988
He was crying really hard.

176
00:10:04,308 --> 00:10:06,908
There were big fat tears all over his face.

177
00:10:07,068 --> 00:10:08,188
And he was sad.

178
00:10:15,148 --> 00:10:15,748
Huh?

179
00:10:16,388 --> 00:10:16,948
Really?

180
00:10:16,948 --> 00:10:17,148
Really?

181
00:10:17,148 --> 00:10:19,368
But what would make Ray cry?

182
00:10:20,108 --> 00:10:22,328
It's probably something he remembered.

183
00:10:29,108 --> 00:10:31,408
A painful memory from the past.

184
00:10:32,208 --> 00:10:32,508
Huh?

185
00:10:36,888 --> 00:10:38,588
I'm sure he misses her.

186
00:10:38,588 --> 00:10:42,848
His own little sister.

187
00:10:49,848 --> 00:10:53,008
One day, my average life as I knew it ended.

188
00:10:53,528 --> 00:10:55,348
As if it had been torn away from me.

189
00:10:55,348 --> 00:11:00,928
When I returned from a school trip, my whole family was suddenly taken from me.

190
00:11:01,408 --> 00:11:03,928
My mom, dad, and little sister.

191
00:11:03,928 --> 00:11:10,368
They were cold, lifeless corpses, frozen in time.

192
00:11:10,368 --> 00:11:21,728
They said the truck driver was drunk at the time.

193
00:11:22,168 --> 00:11:24,388
Apparently, the three of them were killed instantly.

194
00:11:24,588 --> 00:11:26,968
Oh, I wonder what will happen to their son.

195
00:11:27,248 --> 00:11:29,188
Kiwako will probably take him in, right?

196
00:11:29,188 --> 00:11:32,568
There's no way she would agree to taking care of her nephew.

197
00:11:33,128 --> 00:11:35,548
His grandfather's too old to be of any help.

198
00:11:36,088 --> 00:11:37,328
You damn fool.

199
00:11:38,048 --> 00:11:40,668
What is going to happen to the hospital now?

200
00:11:41,108 --> 00:11:44,548
You finally quit Shugi and took over after my retirement.

201
00:11:45,148 --> 00:11:47,428
I thought everything would turn out okay for us.

202
00:11:47,428 --> 00:11:48,388
There's no need to worry.

203
00:11:48,508 --> 00:11:49,268
It's all right.

204
00:11:49,528 --> 00:11:50,228
You've got me.

205
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:51,468
I'll handle it.

206
00:11:51,688 --> 00:11:54,028
This is exactly what I've been telling you all along.

207
00:11:54,328 --> 00:11:55,848
All you thought of was my brother.

208
00:11:57,308 --> 00:11:58,808
What a pitiful child.

209
00:11:59,748 --> 00:12:00,788
Don't worry, Ray.

210
00:12:01,088 --> 00:12:03,648
I'll make sure you're cared for in a good orphanage.

211
00:12:05,648 --> 00:12:07,228
I wasn't sure what she meant.

212
00:12:07,648 --> 00:12:09,728
I didn't exactly know what an orphanage was.

213
00:12:11,368 --> 00:12:15,808
But until then, no matter how tough school was,

214
00:12:16,368 --> 00:12:21,208
I could always return to my room and relax in the warmth of my solitude.

215
00:12:22,988 --> 00:12:27,208
But if I had to live in an orphanage, all of that would change.

216
00:12:27,208 --> 00:12:30,428
I would lose the privacy I longed to escape to.

217
00:12:31,148 --> 00:12:33,448
Soon, I realized the truth.

218
00:12:34,108 --> 00:12:38,488
Out of every single day and night of the year, I'd never have a moment of relief.

219
00:12:38,488 --> 00:12:42,788
And then, that's when he stepped forward.

220
00:12:45,948 --> 00:12:49,988
Many of my relatives had come to the funeral to pay their respects.

221
00:12:49,988 --> 00:12:55,688
But out of everyone who was there that day, he was the only one.

222
00:12:57,128 --> 00:12:58,608
I felt so relieved.

223
00:12:59,148 --> 00:13:00,088
I wanted to cry.

224
00:13:00,088 --> 00:13:05,668
Like I said, my husband will take care of the hospital.

225
00:13:06,068 --> 00:13:07,368
So mind your own business.

226
00:13:08,748 --> 00:13:10,628
Kiwako has such a terrible attitude.

227
00:13:11,228 --> 00:13:13,168
Of course, she's always been that way.

228
00:13:13,448 --> 00:13:15,608
Shh, don't speak ill in front of the deceased.

229
00:13:15,908 --> 00:13:16,828
I can't help it.

230
00:13:16,828 --> 00:13:25,748
Tell me, Ray.

231
00:13:26,788 --> 00:13:28,648
Do you want to play more Shogi?

232
00:13:30,328 --> 00:13:32,988
In that moment, my life was forever changed.

233
00:13:33,628 --> 00:13:34,688
I became bound.

234
00:13:35,348 --> 00:13:37,328
Eternally bound to the Shogi God.

235
00:13:37,328 --> 00:13:45,548
It was a lie.

236
00:13:46,228 --> 00:13:49,488
It was the first time in my life I lied to live.

237
00:13:51,068 --> 00:13:53,848
After that, there was no going back.

238
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:55,868
My fate was sealed.

239
00:13:56,508 --> 00:13:57,448
The ropes were cut.

240
00:13:57,948 --> 00:13:59,088
And the curtain dropped.

241
00:14:00,968 --> 00:14:04,748
I became the child of a Shogi family.

242
00:14:07,328 --> 00:14:21,428
It's coming undone.

243
00:14:22,048 --> 00:14:23,128
This is no good.

244
00:14:23,648 --> 00:14:24,808
Pulling on it makes it worse.

245
00:14:26,088 --> 00:14:27,308
What do I do now?

246
00:14:27,748 --> 00:14:28,668
I'm not even sure.

247
00:14:37,328 --> 00:14:51,148
Maybe this one.

248
00:14:51,748 --> 00:14:52,328
I wonder.

249
00:14:52,328 --> 00:15:06,688
Awaiting my arrival in that house of Shogi

250
00:15:06,688 --> 00:15:08,948
were the true children of the family

251
00:15:08,948 --> 00:15:12,168
who also aspired to be professional Shogi players.

252
00:15:12,448 --> 00:15:13,928
You think you're so special?

253
00:15:14,188 --> 00:15:15,148
You're just a loser!

254
00:15:15,148 --> 00:15:21,288
Their daughter, Kyoko, was four years older than me.

255
00:15:21,908 --> 00:15:23,868
And their son, Ayumu, was also my age

256
00:15:23,868 --> 00:15:24,848
and in the same grade.

257
00:15:38,908 --> 00:15:39,668
Please, honey.

258
00:15:40,128 --> 00:15:41,988
Don't you think she's been out there long enough?

259
00:15:42,308 --> 00:15:43,128
Not at all.

260
00:15:43,128 --> 00:15:44,968
But Kyoko's just a little girl.

261
00:15:45,068 --> 00:15:46,968
This doesn't have anything to do with Shogi.

262
00:15:47,428 --> 00:15:48,868
How dare she strike an opponent?

263
00:15:49,188 --> 00:15:50,128
But dear...

264
00:15:50,728 --> 00:15:52,788
The father was very strict with Kyoko.

265
00:15:54,228 --> 00:15:56,948
I think he was harder on her

266
00:15:56,948 --> 00:15:59,288
because she was so strong.

267
00:15:59,848 --> 00:16:02,048
She was like an untamed storm in every way.

268
00:16:02,328 --> 00:16:03,508
Wild and unpredictable.

269
00:16:04,688 --> 00:16:06,628
Her Shogi, her disposition,

270
00:16:07,248 --> 00:16:08,468
and her beauty as well.

271
00:16:08,468 --> 00:16:10,748
What do you want?

272
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:12,988
Do you have something to say to me, you little punk?

273
00:16:18,628 --> 00:16:19,788
Knock it off, Kyoko!

274
00:16:21,848 --> 00:16:22,968
Um, father?

275
00:16:23,528 --> 00:16:23,968
Uh-huh?

276
00:16:24,328 --> 00:16:25,528
Would you like some more?

277
00:16:26,308 --> 00:16:27,568
Yes, please.

278
00:16:27,568 --> 00:16:32,288
What did you just say to him?

279
00:16:32,668 --> 00:16:34,228
What do you mean, father?

280
00:16:35,168 --> 00:16:37,688
I mean, I'm sorry.

281
00:16:37,948 --> 00:16:38,648
