The three of us stopped spending time together.

349
00:20:06,308 --> 00:20:11,328
It was more than I could take, so I escaped by becoming absorbed into the game.

350
00:20:12,008 --> 00:20:17,748
Then, by the end of my second year in middle school, I was one step away from going pro.

351
00:20:18,308 --> 00:20:20,208
I had reached the third Den League.

352
00:20:20,208 --> 00:20:28,228
This species of bird does not raise its young, but instead engages in what's called brood parasitism.

353
00:20:28,608 --> 00:20:32,908
The cuckoo lays its eggs in the nests of other birds, like shrikes or meadow buntings.

354
00:20:33,068 --> 00:20:39,328
Then, before they've hatched, the cuckoo chick tosses the original eggs out of the nest before their true parents return from hunting.

355
00:20:40,068 --> 00:20:41,788
Then, takes over the nest.

356
00:20:41,788 --> 00:20:49,988
When the unsuspecting parents return, they work tirelessly to feed and raise the chicks, not knowing they're of the bird that murdered their offspring.

357
00:20:50,488 --> 00:20:52,008
Oh, just like me.

358
00:20:52,228 --> 00:20:55,928
Eventually, the cuckoo chick fills the nest and outgrows its surrogate parents.

359
00:20:56,348 --> 00:20:59,748
Even so, the parent continues feeding and nurturing the chick.

360
00:21:00,308 --> 00:21:02,448
That bird is me.

361
